{
  "note": "Originals are kept byte for byte (JPG) or as lossless WebP (PNG converted without any change to pixels). Never delete or replace a sheet; add new ones.",
  "groups": {
    "slomatt/early-hero-sheets": "Slomatt pose and character sheets from the original hero build (magenta-keyed KlingAI / Gemini sheets, including the run, kick, punch, climb, rope and expression sheets the in-game hero atlas was cut from)",
    "jennifur": "Jennifur emotion sheets: sad / crying / dejected walk / celebration / jubilant, and scared / panic (pink headband, #07 vest)",
    "slomatt-and-jennifur": "Slomatt and Jennifur together: hugging, hand-in-hand, conversational gestures, 16 Slomatt expressions, and the core movement and combat sheet (walk, jump, land, punch, kick, crouch, hurt, stunned, knockback, defeated) drawn for both",
    "slomatt/standard-set": "Slomatt standard set (2026-10-20): nine 4x4 sheets on flat grey, no borders or numbers, one subject per sheet, see README for the 12-sheet standard. 144 frames, ~240 px tall; satchel and wrist wraps, no green backpack",
    "slomatt/standard-set-v2": "Slomatt standard set, second round (2026-10-20 evening): nine sheets drawn after a fix to the sheet generation. Heads in profile for side-on frames, white background, character 173-202 px tall (varies by sheet). 02a and 02b are two takes of the walk and run; 13 (swim, dive, glide), 14 (aim, items, wall, air moves) and 15 (air punch and kick, stomp, bounce, mushroom spring; captioned) are extra sheets. Built into the test hero with `cutStandard.py --set v2`. See the Slomatt Animation Sheets audit doc.",
    "story": "Story sheets (2026-10-21): 18 Gemini 4x4 grids on flat grey for the cutscenes: the pink-headband #07 sloth (MEECA, though files 01-04, 13, 14 are named pokey): faces, emotion, action, music-box poses, shut in a room; the satchel sloth (POKEY, though files 10-12 are named meeca): plain, with the bow, wrist-wrapped, Pokey and Meeca together and hugging, Pokey shut in a room, Grandma, the General (armor cracking to tunic; grey tunic; younger in a tan shirt; all a mandrill), Lt. Pell, the town crier and the mail carrier. Cut into the game's story atlases by the story cutter (see README).",
    "pokey-swim": "Pokey swimming for World 6 (2026-10-27, generated, not Matt-supplied, not yet in the game): cut-out frames of surf (surface crawl loop), under (underwater glide loop), tread (tread-water idle loop) and first (first-swim one-shot), scaled to the standard hero; meta.json gives each move its frames, size, anchor (ay = waterline) and fps. Made by tools/art/w6/swim/ (cut.py, picks.json); raw clips are in the HF bucket mshaffe111/w5-xfer under w6swim/clips/."
  },
